-- rows of the representing problem has no model. The certificate is LRAT from CaDiCaL,
-- trimmed (713 steps, 16062 hints, 2 segment(s), solver options --unsat --shrink=0 --reverse=1).
-- It is stored as codes of variable length: dec turns a list of words into the token
-- list of the checker of the LRAT library (one token per word for runW, below a top
-- bit), inside the kernel. The soundness of the checker holds for every token list
-- and every list of live clauses, so dec and ent need no proof.

